<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert Kwok</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1921–1944</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert Kwok was a Chinese resistance leader in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">North Borneo</a> during the Japanese occupation. He organised the Kinabalu <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">Guerrillas</a> and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kota-kinabalu">Jesselton</a> Revolt of October 1943, in which rebels attacked Japanese posts in Jesselton, now Kota Kinabalu. The Japanese crushed the rising and carried out mass reprisals, and Kwok was executed in January 1944.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-kwok.jpg" alt="Albert Kwok" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AlbertKwok.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
